Subject: [PATCH] nexmon: match the 6.12.115 set_monitor_channel prototype

Local compatibility patch for this project (packages/espnow-nexmon), not
upstream. Kali's brcmfmac-nexmon 6.12.2 gates the monitor-channel callback
on LINUX_VERSION_CODE < 6.13.0 and uses the old two-argument form
(wiphy, chandef). The 6.12.115 stable kernel changed cfg80211_ops
.set_monitor_channel to take a struct net_device * as well, so the driver
no longer compiles on 6.12.115 ("initialization ... from incompatible
pointer type").

The gate is moved to 6.12.115, the kernel this image pins. Kernels older
than that keep the old form. The new branch has the same body; the
net_device argument is unused, as before.

--- a/brcmfmac-nexmon-dkms-fff319040f6a8034fce36f846cce2dc19de1b396/cfg80211.c
+++ b/brcmfmac-nexmon-dkms-fff319040f6a8034fce36f846cce2dc19de1b396/cfg80211.c
@@ -765,7 +765,7 @@
 }
 
 #ifdef NEXMON_MON_IF
-#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6,13,0)
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6,12,115)
 static s32
 brcmf_cfg80211_nexmon_set_channel(struct wiphy *wiphy,struct cfg80211_chan_def *chandef) {
 #else
